## Python Instruction
Write a python function to find the first missing positive integer in an unsorted array.

## Python Solution
```python
def find_FirstMissingPositive(nums):
    if not nums:
        return 1
    n = len(nums)
    for i in range(n):
        while 1 <= nums[i] <= n and nums[nums[i] - 1] != nums[i]:
            nums[nums[i] - 1], nums[i] = nums[i], nums[nums[i] - 1]
    for i in range(n):
        if nums[i] != i + 1:
            return i + 1
    return n + 1
```

